{title: Scarborough Fair}
{composer: Traditional}
{key: Am}
{genre: Folk}
{language: English}

{section: Verse 1}
Are you [Am]going to [G]Scarborough [Am]Fair
[C]Parsley [Am]sage rose[D]mary and [Am]thyme
Re[Am]member me to [C]one who lives [G]there
[Am]She once [G]was a true love of [Am]mine

{section: Verse 2}
Tell her to [Am]make me a [G]cambric [Am]shirt
[C]Parsley [Am]sage rose[D]mary and [Am]thyme
With[Am]out no seams nor [C]needle [G]work
[Am]Then she'll [G]be a true love of [Am]mine

{section: Verse 3}
Tell her to [Am]find me an [G]acre of [Am]land
[C]Parsley [Am]sage rose[D]mary and [Am]thyme
Be[Am]tween the salt [C]water and the [G]sea strand
[Am]Then she'll [G]be a true love of [Am]mine
